* CD4007 discrete MOSFETs (one N and one P device of the CD4007UB array)
* Level-1 models. KP, VTO, LAMBDA and W/L are the values in the team's
* device-characterization notes (kn'=70uA/V^2, Vtn=1.4 V, W/L=170u/10u, lambda=0.016;
* kp'=15uA/V^2, Vtp=-1.65 V, W/L=360u/10u, lambda=0.01). These reproduce the
* Multisim operating point (I_tail 701 uA, VG1 2.21 V) to within a few percent.
* Capacitances are estimates sized so the open-loop input |Z| at 200 kHz is near the
* ~1.6 pF the Multisim run implies (491.6 kOhm at 200 kHz); they are NOT vendor data.
* Use: M<name> d g s b CD4007N W=170u L=10u   /  CD4007P W=360u L=10u
.model CD4007N NMOS (LEVEL=1 VTO=1.4 KP=70u LAMBDA=0.016 GAMMA=0 PHI=0.6
+ TOX=1e-7 CGSO=4e-9 CGDO=4e-9 CBD=2p CBS=2p)
.model CD4007P PMOS (LEVEL=1 VTO=-1.65 KP=15u LAMBDA=0.01 GAMMA=0 PHI=0.6
+ TOX=1e-7 CGSO=4e-9 CGDO=4e-9 CBD=2p CBS=2p)
